{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2017-248", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/248", "wordCount": 2205, "segments": [{"start": 27.0, "text": "Hello, and welcome to"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "Localization Best Practices on"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "tvOS."}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "My name is Joaquim Lobo Silva,"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "and over the next few minutes,"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "I'm going to walk you through some of the steps you'll want to"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "take to build a great localized"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "application experience on tvOS."}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "Apple TV is available in"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "multiple languages and regions."}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "And new in tvOS 11, is the"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "addition of Arabic and Hebrew"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "and selectable system languages."}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "Adding international support to"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "your app, is an incredible"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "opportunity to reach new markets"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "and enable more users to use and"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "enjoy your content."}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "And we have a wide variety of"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "APIs and tools to help you do"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "just that."}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "Let's dive right in."}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "I'm going to divide this topic"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "into three different sections."}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "First, I'll talk about best"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "practices on how to handle text"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "that is displayed to your user."}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "Then, I'll cover some"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "considerations regarding layout"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "and images."}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "And finally, the steps needed to"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "export your localizable content,"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "as well as test your app, to"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "make sure it all works."}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "So, let's get started with text."}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "Any text that will be presented"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "to your user, should be"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "displayed in their preferred"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "language."}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "If you have text in Storyboard"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "elements, there's nothing else"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "you need to do."}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "These are marked \"localizable\""}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "by default."}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "If you have strings and code"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "that you're planning on"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "presenting, these should be"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "wrapped with a call to"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "\"NSLocalizedString.\""}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "This will essentially mark your"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "string as \"localizable,\" so that"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "it is included in the file that"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "you will send out for"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "translation."}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "In both of these cases, comments"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "on the strings themselves, are"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "extremely useful, and should be"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "included as part of every"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "localizable string in your app."}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "Comments can be the defining"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "factor between great translated"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "content and text that feels"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "unnatural or unclear."}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "Here's an example of a localized"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "string in code."}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "As you can see, this is simply"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "the English word \"subscribe\""}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "with a comment describing where"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "it will appear in my UI, as well"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "as what it does within the"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "context of my app."}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "Comments are just as easy to add"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "to Storyboard elements as well."}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "For every element, you can"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "simply add a comment in the"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "Comment for Localizer text"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "field, in the Identity"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "Inspector."}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "Do note that when it comes to"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "displaying text in your app,"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "localized strings are not the"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "only way to accomplish this."}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "In fact, it's very likely that"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "you have a number of use cases"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "that are covered by our"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "formatted classes."}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "These help you format and"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "display things like numbers,"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "currencies, dates, units such as"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "length and mass, and much more,"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "without having to write out"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "localized strings for these."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "Here's an example of date"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "formatted usage."}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "I simply create the object, and"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "in this case, I only care about"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "showing time, so I set the Time"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "Style to a length value of my"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "preference, and finally get a"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "formatted string out of the"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "object."}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "This string is guaranteed to not"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "only be in the user's preferred"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "language, but it also takes care"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "of a number of other formatting"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "contexts, such as whether the"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "user prefers 12 or 24-hour time."}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "For much more information on how"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "to make the most out of"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "formatters, as well as some"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "guidance on their international"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "prowess, I highly recommend you"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "check out these two talks from"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "2016."}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "Let's talk about remote content."}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "Any text that you're fetching"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "from a server, should also match"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "your app's running language."}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "I'm referring to, for example,"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "media content and descriptions"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "that are shown in your app."}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "For this to happen, you'll need"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "to inform your server what"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "language the content should"}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "actually be in."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "We have APIs that let you know"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "what language you're app is"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "currently running in, and these"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "do a lot of the heavy lifting in"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "terms of choosing the best"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "language out of the ones that"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "you support, while respecting"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "the user's preferences."}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "Things like regional variance"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "and any appropriate regional"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "fallbacks, are also considered."}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "Just to give a few small"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "examples, I have here a table"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "where the first column shows a"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "language that the user might"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "have picked for their system language."}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "The second column shows"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "potential languages that your"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "application supports, and the"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "third column would be the end"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "result, given the circumstances."}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "For the first example, the user"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "has picked Spanish as their"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "language, with their region set"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "to Mexico, hence the \"es-MX\""}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "identifier."}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "The app supports both Spanish"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "for Spain, as well as Latin"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "American Spanish and the list of"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "localizations, that's \"es-EX\""}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "and \"es-419\" respectively."}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "And the runtime will go ahead"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "and pick the Latin American"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "Spanish variant for your app."}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "Similarly, for the second"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "example, the user has picked"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "Chinese with the region set to"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "China, and Bundle will go ahead"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "and pick \"Simplified Chinese\""}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "out of the languages that your"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "app supports."}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "To get the language that your"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "app is running in, all you have"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "to do is get the first object of"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "preferred localizations from"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "your app's bundle."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "This will return a language"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "identifier that you can send to"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "your server."}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "Alternatively, if your server"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "supports a different set of"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "languages relative to your app,"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "you can also get the best"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "possible language match out of"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "those, using Bundle's Preferred"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "Localizations from Available."}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "So, that's an overview of how to"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "handle text in your app."}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "Text can be marked as"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "localizable through using"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "Storyboards, as well as calling"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "NSLocalizedString and code."}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "We have a number of formatters"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "that help display and"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "contextualize information, like"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "dates and numbers."}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "For remote content, you can rely"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "on the Bundle API to help inform"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "your server what language your"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "content should be displayed in."}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "With that, let's talk a little"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "about layout and images."}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "When it comes to layout, there"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "are typically two different"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "aspects to adapt for."}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "The first one is potential"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "differences in word length."}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "For example, here's the word"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "\"backup\" in English, and here's"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "that same word in Finnish."}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "Translations being significantly"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "longer or shorter, can impact"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "the way your layout behaves at"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "runtime, and you should design"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "for this accordingly."}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "The other aspect is script"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "directionality."}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "English uses the Latin alphabet,"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "which is read and parsed from"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "left to right."}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "Some languages like Arabic, have"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "their scripts read from right to"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "left."}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "As a result, there are a number"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "of design considerations"}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "regarding flow and ordering of"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "information."}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "For example, in a right to left"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "language, the first item in a"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "list is expected to be in the"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "far right, as opposed to the far"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "left."}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "If your app uses UIKit to"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "display user interface elements,"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "there are a few technologies"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "that you can use to easily adapt"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "for these two different aspects."}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "It's highly recommended that you"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "start off with exploring"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "UIStackView."}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "UIStackView is a streamlined"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "interface for laying out a"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "series of views, either"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "horizontally or vertically."}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "And these can be nested to"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "create complex layouts as shown"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "here. In this example, you can see"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "that I have some numbered views,"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "and the general flow of"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "information here is left to"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "right, as expected for a"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "language like English."}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "The thing about UIStackView is"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "that under the hood, it relies"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "on something called Auto Layout."}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "Auto Layout is a set of APIs"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "that help determine layout"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "relationships between views,"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "such that if the size of a view"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "changes, other views can adapt"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "accordingly to prevent overlap"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "or truncation."}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "In addition to this, Auto Layout"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "also relies on the concept of"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "leading and trailing"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "constraints."}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "These are essentially left and"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "right position constraints, but"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "that evaluate to right and left"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "when running in a right to left"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "language."}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "So, for the stack views above,"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "the layout would automatically"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "change to right to left, when"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "running in, for example, Arabic"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "or Hebrew. And this can be accomplished"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "without having to write a single"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "line of extra code for different"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "layout environments."}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "For apps using TVMLKit, the"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "standard templates provided do"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "all the heavy lifting for the"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "two aspects I mentioned."}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "In particular for right to left"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "languages, once again, with the"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "addition of Arabic and Hebrew"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "and selectable system languages,"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "we have some new APIs that"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "leverage the same concept of"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "leading and trailing for TVMLKit"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "elements that have a specific"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "position or alignment."}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "Similarly, for margins and"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "padding, we have new media"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "queries to help specify custom"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "values for a specific layout"}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "direction."}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "To explore these new features in"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "depth, please be sure to check"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "out Advances in TVMLKit."}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "Let's move on to images."}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "And for this, I'm going to"}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "briefly cover an approach to"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "keep in mind for different"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "layout directions."}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "Typically, images in your app"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "will fall into one of three"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "separate buckets."}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "The first one, likely to be most"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "of your images, is universal."}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "These are images that do not"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "need specific adaptation for a"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "layout direction."}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "The second category, is images"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "that do have some direction"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "associated to them."}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "This can be a number of things"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "such as navigation arrows,"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "disclosure indicators, or in"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "this case, a simplified"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "representation of text."}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "The only step required for these"}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "images to adapt for the opposite"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "layout direction, is to"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "graphically mirror them."}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "And now, we have the correct"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "result."}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "Lastly, the third category is"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "similar to the second, but these"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "are relatively complex such that"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "simply flipping them would"}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "actually produce an incorrect"}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "result."}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "In this example, I've a bulleted"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "list with checkmarks, but"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "checkmarks as a symbol should"}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "not be mirrored."}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "So, in this case, what I really"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "need is two separate images, one"}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "for each layout direction."}, {"start": 606.0, "text": "Xcode makes it very easy to"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "handle all of these cases, right"}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "from within your Asset Catalog."}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "For each asset, you can specify"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "whether or not an image has a"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "fixed direction or if it should"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "adapt either through mirroring"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "or through specifying different"}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "images."}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "Then, it's simply a matter of"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "using images regularly either in"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "code or in Interface Builder, as"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "usual."}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "For much more information on how"}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "to use asset catalogs for"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "different layout directions,"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "please check out this talk from"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "2016."}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "So, that's layout and images."}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "We've seen how both UIKit and"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "TVMLKit have very high-level"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "approaches for adaptive layouts,"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "as well as some of the new APIs"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "introduced in tvOS 11 for right"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "to left support."}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "And also, the concept of image"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "directionality and how this is"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "part of image assets."}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "Last but not least, let's cover"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "how you can actually add a"}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "language to your app, from start"}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "to finish."}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "Adding a language to your"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "project is done in the Project"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "Editor."}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "Select your project file from"}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "within Xcode, and in the Project"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "Settings, you can add supported"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "languages in the Localization"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "section."}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "Xcode will manage and keep track"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "of any applicable file"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "management, such as extracting"}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "text from Storyboards, as well"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "as strings you've marked as"}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "localizable in code."}, {"start": 687.0, "text": "When you're ready to send your"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "app's content out for"}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "translation, this is as simple"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "as selecting your project file"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "in Xcode, and choosing Export"}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "for Localization in the Editor"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "menu."}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "Xcode will generate a"}, {"start": 698.0, "text": "translation interchange file, or"}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "XLIFF, for you to send out for"}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "translation."}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "Once you have this file back,"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "reimporting this content into"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "your Xcode project is just a"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "matter of selecting Import"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "Localizations from that same"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "menu."}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "Xcode will update all of the"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "relevant files and resources to"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "make sure that when your app is"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "built, all up to date supported"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "translations are included."}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "Once this is done, it's a good"}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "idea to test your app in the"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "different environments that"}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "you're planning on supporting."}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "Xcode provides a number of"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "different features to help you"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "do this, and you can get a good"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "idea of how your app behaves in"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "these circumstances, even if you"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "don't speak the languages you"}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "support. For Objective-C code, the Static"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "Analyzer supports making sure"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "that any string you provide to a"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "UI element is appropriately"}, {"start": 751.0, "text": "marked as \"localizable.\""}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "Not only that, you can also"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "check if any of your localized"}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "strings are missing comments."}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "For running your app in"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "different languages, there's a"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "convenient set of options for"}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "simulating a specific language"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "or region setting."}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "In addition to this, Xcode also"}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "lets you run your app in a"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "simulated environment, or pseudo"}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "language, such as right to left,"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "so that you can continue testing"}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "your app in your base language,"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "but also see how it would look"}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "like in a right to left"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "language."}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "This can be done in the Options"}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "tab of the Scheme Editor for"}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "your app."}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "The Localizing with Xcode 9"}, {"start": 789.0, "text": "session, covers all of these"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "features and much more for"}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "getting the most out of the tool"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "set when preparing your app for"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "localization."}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "And that's an overview of"}, {"start": 798.0, "text": "localizing and testing your"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "application, from within Xcode."}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "We've seen how you can add"}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "supported languages to your"}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "project, integrate translations,"}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "as well as checking your project"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "and app out in different"}, {"start": 809.0, "text": "environments."}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "For more information and"}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "resources on localization,"}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "please check out the link for"}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "the session."}, {"start": 819.0, "text": "In addition to these resources,"}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "if you're interested in a deeper"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "exploration of localization and"}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "internationalization topics, the"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "sessions listed are a great"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "place to start."}]}
